      "body": "## Summary\nThis PR adds clarity to the quickstart documentation for Apple Silicon (vLLM-Metal) users by:\n\n1. **Enhanced compatibility warning** at the top of the quickstart explaining that vLLM-Metal uses MLX (not PyTorch) and requires MLX-optimized models\n2. **Model compatibility note** in the offline inference section warning users that standard models like `facebook/opt-125m` won't work with Metal backend\n3. **Recommended alternative** pointing users to MLX-community models from Hugging Face\n\n## Fixes\n#50165\n\n## Testing\nThis is a documentation-only change with no code impact.",
